      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "view-switch",
      "description": "Pressed state distinguishes the selected repository representation.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-switch\" aria-label=\"Repository visualization\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">3D</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">List</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-switch{display:inline-flex;padding:3px;border:1px solid var(--line,#dedbe5);border-radius:8px;background:#eeebf3}.ds-switch button{font-family:'Manrope Variable',sans-serif;font-size:10px;border:0;background:transparent;border-radius:5px;padding:7px 10px;color:#756b80;cursor:pointer}.ds-switch button[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:white;color:var(--ink,#302a3b);box-shadow:0 2px 4px #30223a09}.ds-switch button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ds-focus,#9477b5);outline-offset:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Information panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "information-panel",
      "description": "Flat bordered surface for methodology and repository details.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2>Public evidence, not a score</h2><p>Parallax compares visible GitHub work. Stars show interest, not code quality.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:'Manrope Variable',sans-serif;padding:26px;background:var(--paper,#fff);border:1px solid var(--line,#dedbe5);border-radius:var(--radius,12px);color:var(--ink,#302a3b)}.ds-panel h2{font-size:17px;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0;font-weight:700}.ds-panel p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--muted,#716b7a);max-width:65ch}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Owner comparison table",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Semantic owner headings preserve attribution independently of series color.",
      "html": "<table class=\"ds-insights\"><caption>Additional public profile metrics</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Measure</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"ds-a\">Profile A</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"ds-b\">Profile B</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Public gists</th><td class=\"ds-a\">12</td><td class=\"ds-b\">8</td></tr></tbody></table>",
      "css": ".ds-insights{font-family:'Manrope Variable',sans-serif;width:100%;table-layout:fixed;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}.ds-insights caption{font-size:11px;text-align:left;color:var(--muted,#716b7a);padding:0 0 12px}.ds-insights thead{background:#f9f8fb}.ds-insights th,.ds-insights td{padding:12px 6px;font-size:11px;overflow-wrap:anywhere;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#dedbe5)}.ds-insights th:first-child{width:44%;padding-left:0}.ds-insights tbody th{color:var(--muted,#716b7a);font-weight:400}.ds-insights td{font-weight:650;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-a{color:var(--a,#a94235)}.ds-b{color:var(--b,#16776b)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Material atlas",
    "overview": "The Material atlas makes two public bodies of work tangible. Aubergine navigation organizes a cool lilac workspace; coral and teal consistently identify the two sides. Compact typography, aligned quantities and conventional controls keep the interface useful for close comparison.\n\nDepth belongs to the repository landscape. Its paired plinths and rounded columns are rendered from loaded repository data, while exact values remain available in tables. The identity is code-led: an authored geometric SVG mark, self-hosted Manrope and real data geometry. Public GitHub avatars are externally loaded identity images; there are no shipped decorative raster assets.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool lilac ground with a dark aubergine navigation rail.",
      "Coral and teal paired with explicit owner labels.",
      "Compact Manrope typography and tabular numeric alignment.",
      "Data-bound 3D beside conventional tables and controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "Identity with Labels",
        "body": "Series color reinforces an owner name or A/B identifier; it does not replace that label.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Comparable Quantities",
        "body": "Align numbers with tabular figures and give each comparative column an explicit owner.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "Data Makes the Depth",
        "body": "The landscape geometry expresses loaded repository measurements; precise values and repository actions remain available outside the canvas.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep coral and teal paired with A/B identifiers or visible profile names.",
      "Do preserve the visible Compare action across viewport sizes.",
      "Do use semantic row and column headers for comparative numbers.",
      "Do disclose loaded coverage and scale beside the visual that uses them.",
      "Do retain the List alternative, visible focus and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "Do use public GitHub avatars only as identity content and keep authored branding as SVG."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't interpret stars, event counts or landscape height as a developer ability score.",
      "Don't replace precise repository records with a canvas-only interaction.",
      "Don't silently normalize the two activity charts to different scales.",
      "Don't turn every flat information surface into a floating 3D card.",
      "Don't treat decorative color or hover tooltips as the sole carrier of essential information."
    ]
  }
}
